      "created_at": "2015-10-30T21:40:40.000Z",
      "cooked": "<ol>\n<li><span>You are allowed to play cards that go next to another card when there are no applicable cards to do so (for example, Wrest the Mind with no non-character targets in play). The card goes to the trash but is not destroyed.</span></li>\n<li><span>Expatriette’s Ammo cards can be played without a gun in play. If that happens, the Ammo card is destroyed.</span></li>\n</ol><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span>The above two rulings seem inconsistent. Am I missing something?</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
      "post_number": 1,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:45:44.742Z",
