      "raw": "<ol><li><span style=\"color: rgb(51, 51, 51); font-family: 'Open Sans', HelveticaNeue, 'Helvetica Neue', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14.4px; line-height: 21.6px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">You are allowed to play cards that go next to another card when there are no applicable cards to do so (for example, Wrest the Mind with no non-character targets in play). The card goes to the trash but is not destroyed.</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(51, 51, 51); font-family: 'Open Sans', HelveticaNeue, 'Helvetica Neue', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14.4px; line-height: 21.6px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">Expatriette&rsquo;s Ammo cards can be played without a gun in play. If that happens, the Ammo card is destroyed.</span></li></ol><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(51, 51, 51); font-family: 'Open Sans', HelveticaNeue, 'Helvetica Neue', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14.4px; line-height: 21.6px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">The above two rulings seem inconsistent. Am I missing something?</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
